#---
# purpose: "Enum tier-0 functions return Elixir-style public values across List, Range, and Map"
# oracle: oracle.exs
# timeout.interp_secs: 15
# defer.build: two live blockers: Enum.reduce/2 over Map (fz-bfh.3) then fz-k22 (unbound backend value)
# defer.interp: two live blockers: Enum.reduce/2 over Map (fz-bfh.3) then fz-k22 (unbound backend value)
# defer.run: two live blockers: Enum.reduce/2 over Map (fz-bfh.3) then fz-k22 (unbound backend value)
#---
#
# Exercises the reduce-based public `Enum` surface that later Enum functions build
# on: `reduce/2`, `reduce/3`, `reduce_while/3`, `each/2`, `count/1`, `count/2`,
# `member?/2`, `to_list/1`, and `reverse/1,2`. The reduce family runs over List,
# Range, and Map so the "across List, Range, and Map" claim is exercised, not just
# asserted.
#
# ## Why this is still deferred (re-triaged 2026-08-24)
#
# Two of the four originally-cited blockers are CLOSED (fz-bfh.1 reduce/3 over
# Range, fz-bfh.4 range+map storm) and fz-bfh.2's two symptoms both pass in
# isolation at HEAD. What actually stops this fixture now, in order:
#
#   1. `Enum.reduce(map, fn ...)` -- reduce/2 with no accumulator over a Map --
#      raises `Enum.EmptyError`. Elixir yields `{3, :one}`. reduce/3 over Map
#      works, so this is the remaining half of fz-bfh.3.
#   2. With that one line skipped the fixture prints eight more correct values
#      and then dies with `backend value 0 is unbound`, which is fz-k22's
#      signature.
#
# So this is two bugs from green, and both are named. Do not re-triage from the
# original four-ticket list.

fn main() do
  xs = [1, 2, 3, 4]
  range = 1..7//2
  map = %{2 => :two, 1 => :one}

  # reduce/2 across List, Range, and Map
  dbg(Enum.reduce(xs, fn (x, acc) -> x * acc end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(range, fn (x, acc) -> x * acc end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(map, fn ({k, _v}, {ak, av}) -> {ak + k, av} end))
  # reduce/3 across List, Range, and Map
  dbg(Enum.reduce(xs, 0, fn (x, acc) -> acc + x end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(range, 0, fn (x, acc) -> acc + x end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(map, 0, fn ({k, _v}, acc) -> acc + k end))
  # reduce_while/3 across List, Range, and Map
  dbg(Enum.reduce_while(xs, 0, fn (x, acc) ->
    if x < 3 do
      {:cont, acc + x}
    else
      {:halt, acc}
    end
  end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce_while(range, 0, fn (x, acc) ->
    if x < 5 do
      {:cont, acc + x}
    else
      {:halt, acc}
    end
  end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce_while(map, [], fn ({k, v}, acc) ->
    if k < 2 do
      {:cont, [v | acc]}
    else
      {:halt, acc}
    end
  end))
  dbg(Enum.each([:a, :b], fn (x) -> x end))
  dbg(Enum.count(range))
  dbg(Enum.count(xs, fn (x) -> x > 2 end))
  dbg(Enum.member?(range, 5))
  dbg(Enum.member?(range, 6))
  dbg(Enum.member?(map, {1, :one}))
  dbg(Enum.to_list(range))
  dbg(Enum.to_list(map))
  dbg(Enum.reverse(xs))
  dbg(Enum.reverse(range, [:tail]))
end
